Subject: [PATCH 29/37] tools/aurora-sep: add deep-idle-check.py

After a reboot into one of the staged test images or the residency test
kernel, it names the m1n1 image by its sha256 and reports whether the
change took: CPU opp-microwatt in the live device tree, the energy
model's performance domains, the pmp and dcpext aliases, whether
apple_pmp bound, the cpuidle settings and residency, and the display,
ANE, USB-C and PMP power domains. It only reads; the debugfs parts need
root.

